---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, phoneHref } from '../data/site';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy policy | Beermat Studio"
  description="How Beermat Studio looks after your details when you use the enquiry form or visit this website."
  path="/privacy"
  solidHeader
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1 class="h1">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Short version: I only use your details to reply to you and to see which ads work. I don’t sell your data.
      </p>

      <h2>Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        Beermat Studio is run by {site.founder} in {site.town}.
        {site.legalLine && <> {site.legalLine}</>}
        You can contact me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>{site.phone && <> or on <a href={phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a></>}.
      </p>

      <h2>The enquiry form</h2>
      <p>
        When you send the form I collect your name, pub name, town, phone number, email address and the number of pubs you run.
        I use them to reply to your enquiry and to talk to you about a website for your pub. My lawful basis is legitimate interests,
        because you asked me to get in touch.
      </p>
      <p>
        The form also records which ad or link brought you here (the campaign details in the web address), the page you landed on and
        where you came from. I use this to understand which marketing works.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your enquiry is sent by email using Resend, which processes it on my behalf. I keep enquiries for as long as I need them to
        deal with your request and for a reasonable period after, and then delete them. You can ask me to delete yours at any time.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no analytics or advertising cookies unless you press “Accept” on the cookie banner.
        If you accept, I load Google Analytics (GA4) to count visits and clicks, and the Meta Pixel to measure
        how many people who see my ads send an enquiry. These tools set cookies and may send data to Google and Meta.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you accept, then submit the form, I may also send a Lead event to Meta’s Conversions API.
        That includes your email address and phone number in a hashed (scrambled) form, so Meta can match the enquiry to an ad.
        I don’t do this if you decline cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can change your mind at any time using “Cookie settings” in the footer. To remove cookies that are already set,
        clear this site’s cookies in your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct or delete the personal data I hold about you, and you can object to how I use it.
        Email me and I’ll deal with it. If you’re unhappy, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated: November 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
